 destroy humanity  the biggest comparison that we always  keep hearing about is lelouch  from code geass as it's been over a  decade since code geass finished airing  i don't mind discussing the ending here  in code geass the main character ends up  turning himself  into a villain in order to turn all the  hatred of the world upon himself  his main goal is to stop the constant  war and suffering that the people of the  world have been dealing with  and the way that he chooses to do that  is by uniting all the different nations  and factions of the world  in their opposition to him once everyone  starts seeing him  as the main threat to global peace  lelouch orchestrates his own  assassination or pretend assassination  depending on your  interpretation of the ending the world  then watches as this hated villain is  killed before their eyes  and in the aftermath the once warring  nations decide to work together  in order to forge a new and better world  now i'm definitely oversimplifying the  code geass story for the sake of brevity  but the point is that lelouch's story is  a great example of the protagonist  undergoing a drastic character  development  and as aaron has made his own journey  from hero to villain  many have made the comparison between  lelouch and aaron and a lot of people  have speculated that perhaps aaron is  planning something similar to lelouch  if aaron turns himself into the world's  greatest villain and the single biggest  threat  to world peace then maybe all nations  can unite  in order to defeat him including the  aldians  once aaron is defeated maybe the various  nations of the world can finally learn  to live in peace  and since the aldians helped take aaron  down maybe the world will finally learn  to accept them  i thought that this was maybe a possible  endgame for aaron at first  but the more the story has progressed  the less likely this scenario  seems and it is worth noting that in  code geass there is no race of people  who can turn  into titans aaron being defeated would  not change the fact that most of the  world is afraid of aldians as a whole  because of their abilities to turn into  titans in terms of lelouch  he was definitely responsible for the  deaths of many people  including civilians but he didn't launch  a literal global apocalypse that has  already killed  a countless number of people and leveled  nearly an entire continent  if aaron had just taken out a bunch of  military targets  or if he had launched a limited rumbling  i could have seen the lelouch scenario  happening  but after chapter 131 i don't think that  aaron can be put in the same category as  lelouch  aaron has crossed the line and short of  some sort of time travel shenanigans  i don't think that aaron can ever go  back to being a hero who is just  pretending to be a villain  aaron's desire to protect parodies might  be noble  but his actions are the very definition  of super villainy  and chapter 131 really proved it and so  if we're not going towards a code geass  type ending  how will the attack on titan manga  finally end  there are probably three reasonable  possibilities with one additional  wild card option option one is that  aaron really will destroy the whole  world  except for parodies and then after that  he might use the founding titan's power  to erase  everyone's memories of the actual  apocalypse  and this would essentially give everyone  on the island except for aaron himself  a fresh start as they would believe that  they are the only humans  left in the world and since they  wouldn't remember why  they happened to be the only humans left  they wouldn't feel guilty  about what aaron has done option 2 is  that aaron will fail to destroy the  world because the alliance of scouts and  marland warriors  will stop him this option would  definitely give us an absolutely epic  final battle but can we really expect  mikasanarman to  actually go through with killing aaron  i'd have to see it  to believe 